    "Record-only: no quantitative movement or ability expectation is established in docs/behaviour.",
    "Reproduce with recorder seed 12345, pre-staging frame 300, tick zero frame 345, logical cadence 1/30 s; AI suspended and fog revealed.",
    "Record alive, pos.xyz, fwd.xyz, hull and shield each tick. See README.md for measured usability and reproduction.",
    "Original recordings (P2-06, FoC debug build, quick-loaded map, seed 12345, tick 0 at frame 345): three runs agree bit for bit in every field, so the original's spread is 0. Each tolerance is the larger of that spread and the conversion bound (docs/traces.md): the corvette turns without translating, so its position (-1800, -1500, -20), hull (1125) and shield (600) are whole numbers held for the whole recording, exact in binary32 and in Q24, so 0; fwd: yaw passes non-whole binary32 degrees up to 89.25, where binary32 steps by 2^-17 degree and moves a component by up to 2.23 raw, and pitch holds at most 0.115 degree off whole (0.002 raw); with the whole-degree terms (2 pi for the remake's turn quanta, 8.5 for its trig, 1 for the recorder's rounding) the bound is 18.02 raw, below 19. Accumulated integration error of the remake's own turning is not in these bounds and needs its own evidence."
